    "https://www.pacificu.edu/blog/employers-for-portland-area-grads": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Who's Hiring? Finding a Job After College in the Portland Metro | Pacific University Skip to main content Home Search Main navigation Academics Admissions Life at Pacific About Secondary menu Search Main menu (Mobile) Academics Admissions Life at Pacific About Quick links Calendar Athletics Libraries Office Directory Give Information for ... Current Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Community Breadcrumb Blog Posts Who's Hiring? Finding a Job After College In The Portland Metro Who's Hiring? Finding a Job After College in the Portland Metro Paragraphs Jobs for Portland Area College Grads in Almost Every Industry Jump into a career where you can make a difference as soon as possible with Pacific’s Four-Year Graduation Guarantee . Save money and get your degree on time while still receiving the real-world training that sets Boxers apart. Boasting a thriving and diverse job market, the Portland metro area supports both recent graduates looking to kickstart their career and experienced professionals with new training . With a reputation as a hub for innovative healthcare, technology, business and more, jobs in Portland are abundant, with organizations looking for highly-qualified candidates. The hands-on training and rich alumni network baked into every Pacific University degree uniquely prepares you to pursue job opportunities in Portland. This means that you can leverage college internship , volunteer and practicum experience throughout the region to help secure an exciting career, sometimes even before graduating. From Nike to LAIKA, OHSU to Intel, the variety of companies that call Portland home provide numerous opportunities for recent graduates to make an immediate impact . Discover the ways you can put your connections to work and see how getting your degree in the Portland metro area can unlock possibilities in nearly every industry. PLAN A VISIT TO CAMPUS Portland is a Professional Healthcare Hotspot Healthcare jobs in Portland are plentiful, with new roles in professional health settings projected to be the most abundant over the next five years . Those roles span a wide variety of fields and environments, meaning that whatever your passions, you can put them into practice in Portland’s healthcare landscape. Dozens of cutting-edge hospitals, nationally-recognized specialty care centers and interprofessional opportunities are all right in our backyard, making finding a healthcare job near you — and with a Pacific connection — easy. Healthcare industries hiring in Portland include, but are in no way limited to: Dental hygiene . Pacific’s community-minded approach to its dental hygiene degree enables you to form connections with professionals throughout the Portland metro area. This robust network makes finding dental hygienist jobs in Portland simple, with alumni working across the region. Optometry . One of Pacific’s longest-running programs, the OD pathway fills a niche that places graduates into roles almost immediately. Optometrist jobs are on the rise both nationally and in underserved regions across the Pacific Northwest. Occupational and physical therapy . In-demand both in private settings and through medical hospitals, occupational and physical therapy roles are abundant in Portland. Occupational therapy jobs in the Portland metro area are in especially high demand through schools and other specialized environments. Athletic training . As the scope of athletic training broadens to include more environments and applications, so too does the need for qualified professionals . Portland jobs for athletic trainers are on the rise, especially in workplace settings to help prevent repetitive strain injury. Audiology . Community presence and accessibility define Pacific’s audiology program, which places graduates throughout the region and the country. Audiology jobs in the Portland metro area are growing in number, enabling audiology graduates to find employment soon after getting their degree. Multiple large medical campuses — including Oregon Health and Science University, Kaiser Permanente, and Providence — in combination with smaller, private clinics give you almost endless choices when searching for healthcare jobs in Portland. Experienced Educators are In-Demand Throughout Portland Oregon is currently undergoing a teacher shortage , meaning that educators with a variety of professional experience are able to find meaningful roles in settings they’re passionate about. Portland public schools, as well as neighboring school districts in Beaverton and Hillsboro, are full of Pacific alumni making an impact in the lives of young people and their families. Because of the demand for highly-trained teachers, graduates of Pacific’s Master of Arts in Teaching (MAT) program are specially suited to leadership positions in the classroom. With a combination of invaluable hands-on training and opportunities for specialization , Pacific education graduates can secure teaching jobs in Portland at an advanced level. Whether you are an experienced educator looking to hone your skills or a recent graduate beginning a career in the classroom, Portland-area teaching jobs can help you fulfill your passion for helping others. The Next Big Tech Breakthrough Will Call Portland Home Pacific’s location in the heart of the Silicon Forest — a name derived from the high concentration of tech companies in the Portland area — provides unique opportunities for students and graduates to work on cutting-edge projects. Tech companies in the Portland area benefit greatly from the skilled graduates from nearby universities, and Pacific offers the kinds of in-demand programs that can help you get a foot in the door. Degrees and certificates in computer science , engineering physics , data science and more can prepare you to impress some of the top tech companies near Portland, including Intel, Autodesk, Wacom and Apple. Tech companies hiring in the Portland area look for graduates with demonstrated research and leadership skills , something essential to the Pacific experience. The tech sector in the Portland metro area is only getting larger, and through nearby internships and fellowships accessible to Pacific students , taking advantage of that growth is right at your fingertips. From Local to Global: Portland Businesses Seek Change Makers More than just tech companies call the Portland area home. Some of the largest international brands have a major presence in the Northwest, resulting in a demand for skilled expertise. Degrees in economics , communications , psychology , as well as online MBA programs , all provide the skills that brands headquartered in Portland look for. Retailers — like Nike, Columbia and Adidas — manufacturing giants such as Daimler and Precision Castparts , and even publishing juggernauts like Dark Horse Comics call the Portland metro home. The proximity to these organizations gives Pacific grads a leg up in securing a rewarding career, putting their passions into practice and opening the door to career advancement . Uplift Communities in the Portland Area Through Social Services Like most major metropolitan areas, Portland and its surrounding cities require many social services professionals. Social service careers in Portland involve everything from helping underserved communities get access to healthcare to working in schools. Whether as a professional social worker , public health expert or advocate in the criminal justice system , finding careers that match your drive to help others is easy. The Portland metro area offers opportunities for those with advanced training as well, with abundant opportunities for careers in nonprofit leadership and social work in the Portland area. Through municipal organizations, private nonprofits or in healthcare settings, social service workers have options in the Portland metro. Secure your spot in some of the Pacific Northwest’s most acclaimed professional programs with Guaranteed Graduate School Admission at Pacific! INQUIRE TODAY Blog/News Tags Career Development Request info Request info Apply now Apply now Request info Request info Apply now Apply now Footer Menu Support at Pacific Emergency Information Tech Support Newsroom Careers at Pacific Policies & Forms Office Directory Facebook Instagram Youtube Tiktok Linkedin home link 2043 College Way Forest Grove, OR 97116 503-352-6151 Online Privacy Digital Accessibility Non-Discrimination Copyright © Pacific University all rights reserved"
    },
    "https://www.pacificu.edu/directory/division-college-undergraduate-studies/advising-center/employer-resources/post-job": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Post A Job | Pacific University Skip to main content Home Search Main navigation Academics Admissions Life at Pacific About Secondary menu Search Main menu (Mobile) Academics Admissions Life at Pacific About Quick links Calendar Athletics Libraries Office Directory Give Information for ... Current Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Community In this section ... Employer Resources Post A Job Internships Service Work-Study Sponsorships Breadcrumb Office Directory Division & College of Undergraduate Studies Academic & Career Advising Center Information For Employers Post A Job Post A Job Paragraphs If you want to post and advertise an off-campus job opening on Handshake please contact Academic & Career Advising at advisingcenter@pacificu.edu . Pacific University uses HandShake (joinhandshake.com) , a free job posting site for employers. Students and alumni are directed here to search for internships, work-study, summer jobs, part-time jobs, and full-time positions.  We also send Job Blast emails to students with opportunities on a frequent basis. Getting Help with Student Employment Several offices support elements of student employment while at Pacific University—there is not one single office or person in charge.  When you need help with something related to student employment, use the chart below to navigate to the right office to answer your question.  In general, Financial Aid helps students with financial issues and work study eligibility, Academic and Career Advising helps students find opportunities, make the most of college employment for their future careers, and supports faculty and staff in facilitating student employment as a learning opportunity. Human Resources handles questions about Paycom, posting student jobs , hiring/onboarding, time cards, payroll, employment eligibility, and supervising student workers . For questions about... Go to... Student financial aid packages, updates/changes to financial aid, questions on FWS eligibility UG Students Last Name A-L: Griffin Shaulis griffin.shaulis@pacificu.edu UG Students Last Name M-Z: Stacie Englund stacie@pacificu.edu Grad Students: Lisa Christensen Lisa0507@pacificu.edu FWS award letters / certifications Financial Aid Office: financialaid@pacificu.edu FWS and NWS budget allocations Your budget manager Increasing departmental allocation for Federal Work Study Go to your budget manager, who can work with Financial Aid Finding a job, publicizing jobs, off campus jobs, Handshake Academic & Career Advising: advisingcenter@pacificu.edu Career planning, resumes, interviewing Academic & Career Advisors: advisingcenter@pacificu.edu Learning-oriented supervision, experiential learning Stephanie Stokamer, Applied & Experiential Learning: stok@pacificu.edu Paycom onboarding, log in issues, supervisor role issues HRAccount@pacificu.edu , 503-352-3116 Student Employment Information Student payroll related, logging hours, time cards, payroll issues, balance of FWS Student Employment Information Contact Us Academic & Career Advising Pacific Hall 129 | advisingcenter@pacificu.edu Footer Menu Support at Pacific Emergency Information Tech Support Newsroom Careers at Pacific Policies & Forms Office Directory Facebook Instagram Youtube Tiktok Linkedin home link 2043 College Way Forest Grove, OR 97116 503-352-6151 Online Privacy Digital Accessibility Non-Discrimination Copyright © Pacific University all rights reserved"
    },
    "https://www.pacificu.edu/directory/division-college-undergraduate-studies/advising-center/career-planning/find-job": {
      "title": "Main navigation",
      "description": "Find a Job | Pacific University Skip to main content Home Search Main navigation Academics Admissions Life at Pacific About Secondary menu Search Main menu (Mobile) Academics Admissions Life at Pacific About Quick links Calendar Athletics Libraries Office Directory Give Information for ... Current Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Community In this section ... Career Planning Career Advisors Career Resources Find a Job Resume & Cover Letter Writing Internships Work Study Preparing for Grad School Breadcrumb Office Directory Division & College of Undergraduate Studies Academic & Career Advising Center Career Planning Find a Job Find a Job Paragraphs Students and alumni should sign up for Handshake (pacificu.joinhandshake.com) .  Pacific University provides you with this free job search site where you can search for internships, summer jobs, volunteer opportunities, events, and both part-time and full-time jobs.  Employers want to recruit YOU so sign up today! For more information on how to effectively use this resource, view our Starting with Handshake document. Current students should plan to attend the Work & Service Fairs offered during the first week of the semester in Fall and Spring.  Contact advisingcenter@pacificu.edu if you have questions about the upcoming fair. To find work-study and part-time on campus jobs go to pacificu.edu/jobs . SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT Getting Help with Student Employment Several offices support elements of student employment while at Pacific University—there is not one single office or person in charge.  In general, Financial Aid helps students with financial issues and work study eligibility, Academic and Career Advising helps students find opportunities, make the most of college employment for their future careers, and supports faculty and staff in facilitating student employment as a learning opportunity. Human Resources handles questions about Paycom, posting student jobs , hiring/onboarding, time cards, payroll, employment eligibility, and supervising student workers . Job Search Resources There are many online resources to search for jobs in your desired field. We’ve provided a list of well-known sources below. Be sure to check out our guide for writing your resume and cover letter and interviewing as you begin your job search. Indeed Glassdoor LinkedIn Handshake SimplyHired Career Builder CoolWorks Dice Idealist Mac's List Oregon Job Listings Government Jobs US Jobs Work for Good Volunteering in Health Care Public Service Jobs For more career search resources, see our Guide to Finding Job Opportunities or schedule an appointment with a career advisor today! Footer Menu Support at Pacific Emergency Information Tech Support Newsroom Careers at Pacific Policies & Forms Office Directory Facebook Instagram Youtube Tiktok Linkedin home link 2043 College Way Forest Grove, OR 97116 503-352-6151 Online Privacy Digital Accessibility Non-Discrimination Copyright © Pacific University all rights reserved"
    },
    "https://www.pacificu.edu/directory/division-college-undergraduate-studies/advising-center/career-planning/work-study": {
      "title": "Work Study",
      "description": "Work Study | Pacific University Skip to main content Home Search Main navigation Academics Admissions Life at Pacific About Secondary menu Search Main menu (Mobile) Academics Admissions Life at Pacific About Quick links Calendar Athletics Libraries Office Directory Give Information for ... Current Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Community In this section ... Career Planning Career and Experiential Learning Coaching Career Resources Find a Job Resume & Cover Letter Writing Internships Work Study Preparing for Grad School Work Study Paragraphs Banner Image Breadcrumb Office Directory Division & College of Undergraduate Studies Academic & Career Advising Center Career Planning Work Study Federal Work-Study (FWS) is awarded to students by the Office of Financial Aid. Students earn the awarded funds by working part-time jobs. Work-Study is a great way to start to explore career opportunities! Unlike other forms of financial aid, Work-Study is earned and received in the form of bi-weekly paychecks from the University for hours worked in Work-Study jobs. If no work is done, no funds are earned. It does not get applied to tuition or money owed to the college. If you are a Graduate Student with Work Study, begin talking with an Administrative Assistant or representative from your program now to see which work study jobs might be available or will be available soon.  Networking within your department and asking about upcoming open Work Study positions is usually the best way to find an opening! Students will have opportunities to find and apply for Work Study positions through the Virtual Work & Service Fair on Handshake in September. If you have not yet signed up for a Handshake account please do so at pacificu.joinhandshake.com . What is the difference between Work-Study and Non-Work-Study jobs? Not much! The only difference is where the money in your paycheck comes from. Federal Work Study (or, FWS) is part of your financial aid package. You will see more FWS jobs posted because Pacific has a federal work study program. Non-work study jobs (or, NWS) are jobs that are paid from Pacific University departmental budgets instead of part of your federal financial aid package. How do I use my Work-Study? The first step is to apply for a job! Students can find Work-Study jobs readily in almost all departments on campus, and at approved community service partners. You can find job postings at pacificu.edu/jobs ; active jobs will be posted here throughout the school year. One of the greatest sources for finding jobs will be the biannual Work & Service Fairs co-presented by Academic & Career Advising and the Tom McCall Center for Civic Engagement. What if I have financial aid questions about Work Study? In order to be considered for Federal Work-Study, the FAFSA must be filed by March 1 st each year. If you are wondering how much you can earn via work study, please contact Financial Aid . They will have access to your award amounts and aid package. Each student has a dedicated financial aid counselor who is available to answer questions. What do I do after I'm offered a position? The student employment procedures are all completed online via a tool called Paycom.  Please know that all NEW hires will need to complete information for the Federal W4 & I9 forms. The federal I9 form requires that you show us an original identification form (no photos or copies accepted).  The most common ID forms accepted are social security card, US birth certificate or US Passport, but see the complete list on the I9 form itself. For more details about hiring paperwork and Paycom, please contact Human Resources . If you have Paycom questions please submit your question here and someone will respond to you. How do I prepare to apply for jobs? If you would like assistance putting together a competitive application, creating a resume, or help applying for jobs please contact Academic & Career Advising .  We can walk you through the process! Work Study jobs are available all year long, however the community service positions only hire until late October every Fall. How do I actually apply for jobs? Read through the section called Apply for a Pacific University Student Employment Position area on the HR website to learn how to apply for jobs. Jobs for the academic year will be posted at pacificu.edu/jobs . What does the hiring process look like? See the section on Student Employment Hiring Process to see the steps. Can I learn more about the rules and my responsibilities in having a Work-Study job? Yes! Review the Employee Student Guidebook , found on the Human Resources Student Employment webpage. Have additional questions? Here is a link to the frequently asked questions about the Work-Study program. Paycom questions? Please submit your question here and someone will respond to you. Check out our Community Service Work-Study Partners websites: Adelante Mujeres Adventure without Limits Beaverton School District - AVI D City of Cornelius Library City of Hillsboro Community Connection CREATE Program Eden Acres Forest Grove/Cornelius Chamber of Commerce Forest Grove City Library Forest Grove Community School Forest Grove Temporary Emergency Shelter Free Orchards Elementary Girl Scouts of Oregon and SW Washington Harvey Clarke Elementary School Hillsboro School District - AVID HomePlate Youth Services Pacific University Center for a Sustainable Society Pacific University Office of Accessibility & Accomodation (OAA) Services Pacific University McCall Center for Civic Engagement Start Making a Reader Today (SMART) Tom McCall Upper Elementary School Valley Art Association Contact Us Academic & Career Advising advisingcenter@pacificu.edu Melissa Vieira | Associate Director, Academic & Career Advisor 503-352-3126 | melissav@pacificu.edu Stacie Englund | Assistant Director of Financial Aid 503-352-2858 | stacie@pacificu.edu | Marsh Hall , Office of Financial Aid Footer Menu Support at Pacific Emergency Information Tech Support Newsroom Careers at Pacific Policies & Forms Office Directory Facebook Instagram Youtube Tiktok Linkedin home link 2043 College Way Forest Grove, OR 97116 503-352-6151 Online Privacy Digital Accessibility Non-Discrimination Copyright © Pacific University all rights reserved Also of Interest What The F(Ws) Is Work-Study?! Find A Job The Community Service Work-Study Program"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/ABFDAFED645B6920CFDB8559C078F8A5/jobs/266625": {
      "title": "Director, School of Physical Therapy & Athletic Training",
      "description": "Director, School of Physical Therapy & Athletic Training You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director, School of Physical Therapy & Athletic Training Hot Job Hillsboro Professional Campus - Hillsboro, OR 97123-4218 Apply Overview Salary Range $160,000.00 - $170,000.00 Position Type Full Time Apply Description Pacific University achieves excellence and distinction by investing in exceptional people to think, care, create, and pursue justice in our world. We embrace discovery in a close and nurturing environment that leads to genuine transformation. Our community is diverse, sustainable, and dedicated to discovery and excellence in teaching, scholarship, and practice. At Pacific University, we thrive in an extraordinary environment, surrounded by the beauty of the great Pacific Northwest, with campus locations in Forest Grove and Hillsboro. We humbly acknowledge and thank the original caretakers of the lands on which we live, work, teach, and acquire and share knowledge. Description The School of Physical Therapy and Athletic Training houses the Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) and Master of Science in Athletic Training (MSAT) programs. The Director of the School of Physical Therapy and Athletic Training is the chief academic officer for these programs, and also serves as the DPT Program Director. The Director reports to the Vice Provost and Executive Dean of the College of Health Professions, is a member of the College of Health Professions Deans and Directors Council, and serves on University committees. The Director provides leadership and administration for the School, supports the mission of the School and DPT and MSAT programs, promotes a positive and respectful environment for students, faculty and staff, and represents the School in the College, the University, the community, and the profession. The Director is responsible for providing guidance in the development of long-range programmatic planning, goals, and objectives. Responsibilities Provide vision and leadership for the School of Physical Therapy and Athletic Training Foster a community of inclusion in all aspects of departmental functions, including instruction, service, scholarship, advising, administrative work and collaboration with students Develop strong relationships with internal and external parties to promote the DPT and MSAT programs and to support the mission of the School Actively pursue external opportunities for funding, facilities, and research Prepare, manage, and administer program budgets and advocate for economic support Ensure compliance with institutional policies and accreditation standards Facilitate the faculty in long-range planning and program development Guide the faculty in outcomes assessment and curriculum review Contribute to recruitment, supervision, and evaluation of faculty and staff Recruit, supervise, and evaluate administrative personnel Implement standards for student performance and advancement Coordinate fundraising activities in support of programmatic goals Represent the School in the University’s administrative structure Represent the School on local, state, and national levels within the professions and the community Qualifications Required Qualifications PhD, EdD, DSc or similar terminal doctorate degree and to possess or be eligible to hold an Oregon Physical Therapy License.  Applicant holds an active, unencumbered PT license in any United States jurisdiction. Has a minimum of six years of full-time higher education experience, with a minimum of three years of full-time experience as a core faculty member in a CAPTE-accredited entry-level physical therapist education program. Academic experience allowing the candidate to be eligible for Associate or Full Professor status Evidence of increasing administrative, management, and budgetary responsibilities Outstanding leadership, interpersonal, and communication skills Management style which emphasizes open communication, collaborative work relations, and continuous quality improvement Knowledge of curriculum design, outcomes assessment, and accreditation Teaching experience in physical therapy, athletic training, or health care higher education Service to the community and the physical therapy and/or athletic training professions Preferred Qualifications •    Athletic Training degree or background •    Understanding of the profession of Athletic Training and its academic accreditation process APPLICATION PROCESS To apply, please upload your Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter and names and phone numbers of three professional references along with your Paycom application, Please name your documents as shown in the following example: (Example:  Adams_Amy letter, Adams_Amy CV, Adams_Amy references).  Persons who do not follow and complete the application process are not applicants and will not be considered for employment. Only qualified applicants will be contacted for an interview. During the selection process, we will strive to provide timely notifications. The selection process may vary from recruitment to recruitment but typically includes multiple interviews and may take several weeks depending on the position. All qualified applicants will be notified once the selection process has closed. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and continue to work without employer visa sponsorship, now or in the future. At Pacific University, we are dedicated to offering experiences that are authentic, holistic, equity-minded, and responsive. Our communal success rests on the recognition that complex problems and effective solutions are best approached by teams with a variety of diverse perspectives. and life experiences. As we continue to develop our equity practices, we actively promote access to opportunities and equitable pay for all employees. We, who make up Pacific University, aspire to become a community of purpose where everyone is enabled to be wholly and comfortably who they are; accountable for inclusive behaviors and practices; built on trust, civility, care, openness, and honest conversations often around critical subjects. We know that these values are critical to prepare for a global world with complex problems, through an asset-based mindset so that everyone is afforded an opportunity to succeed. We believe in fostering a workplace where every employee is respected, their contributions are valued, and they are provided opportunities to succeed. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS We offer a comprehensive benefits package for qualifying employees. Current benefits include: ●    Generous paid time off (for vacation, holidays—including winter break—and sick leave) ●    Medical coverage with alternative care options (with in-network services covered at 100% after payroll deduction) ●    Comprehensive dental and vision plans ●    Generous retirement contribution after one year of service with no match required ●    Free mental health appointments ●    Tuition remission for employees and their dependent child(ren) who meet eligibility requirements ●    On-campus benefits, including free access to our sports facility and library ●    Discounts on campus food, bookstore purchases, clinic services, and outdoor program gear rentals (including kayaks, snowshoes, and bikes) EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYMENT Pacific University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to complying with all applicable laws, including those concerning employment and workplace policies. We are committed to fostering a non-discriminatory and inclusive work environment. We are proud to encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds, including those from historically underrepresented groups. NOTICE OF NONDISCRIMINATION POLICY Pacific University makes all employment decisions without regard to race, color, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, age, religion or religious creed, disability, sex, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other characteristics protected by applicable law. Applicable laws include, but are not limited to, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination Act, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990. Questions or complaints may be directed to the Vice President for Academic Affairs at 2043 College Way, Forest Grove, OR 97116 or via email at provost@pacificu.edu. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/ABFDAFED645B6920CFDB8559C078F8A5/jobs/194800": {
      "title": "HVAC & Refrigeration Technician",
      "description": "HVAC & Refrigeration Technician You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account HVAC & Refrigeration Technician Hot Job Forest Grove Campus - Forest Grove, OR 97116; Hillsboro Professional Campus - Hillsboro, OR 97123-4218 Apply Overview Salary Range $77,000.00 - $79,163.00 Position Type Exempt Apply Description Pacific University achieves excellence and distinction by investing in exceptional people to think, care, create, and pursue justice in our world. We embrace discovery in a close and nurturing environment that leads to genuine transformation. Our community is diverse, sustainable, and dedicated to discovery and excellence in teaching, scholarship, and practice. At Pacific University, we thrive in an extraordinary environment, surrounded by the beauty of the great Pacific Northwest, with campus locations in Forest Grove, Hillsboro, and Eugene. We humbly acknowledge and thank the original caretakers of the lands on which we live, work, teach, and acquire and share knowledge. GENERAL DESCRIPTION OF POSITION Performs skilled work in maintaining, operating, and repairing of all campus buildings and facilities.  Inspect, repair, install, and maintain physical facilities requiring skilled mechanical and trade work.  Performs work in the inspection, repair, construction and documentation of all work, systems, and hazardous conditions pertaining to HVAC units and their control systems. Responsible for maintaining and repairing all HVAC/Refrigeration equipment and controls in all campus buildings.  Includes all boilers, chillers, heat pumps, packaged units, cooling towers, VAV/VVT units, steam systems and refrigeration equipment.  Responsible for operation, calibration and maintenance of all building control systems, including pneumatic, electric and DDC. Knowledge in Niagra, Mitsubishi, Pelican, Johnson, Compass and Daikin controls is preferred. Will maintain detailed logs of all preventive maintenance and repair activities.  The emphasis is on preventive maintenance. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS/MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES Respond daily to safety and emergency situations regarding students, faculty, and staff. Replace all air filters and fan belts on a scheduled basis. Scheduled inspection, adjustment and calibration of all equipment and controls as per manufacturers’ recommendations. Respond to comfort complaints (i.e., too hot, too cold, odors, etc.). Maintain preventive maintenance logbook and services histories on each piece of equipment. Annual calibration of all pneumatic controls. Clean and service all kitchen refrigeration equipment as needed. Keep all other engineers and campus community informed of work being performed that may impact their living, teaching, or work area. May lead or instruct other workers as required. Ability to work with outside contractors following all University procedures and reporting procedures. Operate hand and power tools in a skilled manner; fabricate material and equipment. SECONDARY FUNCTIONS Perform other related duties as required by the Facilities Engineering Supervisor, Lead Engineer or Director of Facilities and Safety Management. Perform other related duties as assigned. JOB SCOPE The job operates within established parameters; however the individual is responsible for making recommendations and having input on decisions that relate directly to their area of expertise. SUPERVISOR RESPONSIBILITY None Qualifications EDUCATION AND/OR EXPERIENCE Minimum of 5 years of overall related facilities working experience. 5 years overall HVAC/Refrigeration experience (in all aspects of repair and maintenance). 3 years experience with pneumatic control systems. 2 years experience with DDC control systems. 2 years experience with boilers, chillers, cooling towers and packaged units. Licensure required: Oregon Building Codes Division issued LME or LEB Electrical and Universal CFC Refrigeration. Ability to be on-call for emergencies, evenings, weekends, holidays. Excellent oral and written communication skills Excellent customer service skills Experience with minor air balancing a plus. Ability to work in all kinds of weather, noise, odor, dust and temperatures. Valid Oregon Drivers License. Experience with computer-based PM programs is desired. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, ABILITIES & BEHAVIORS Communicates with students, faculty, staff and the public appropriate to the age of the individual served. Builds on basic learning and carries it from one situation to another. Demonstrates critical thinking skills in problem solving and decision-making. Asks questions and seeks assistance. Takes responsibility to eliminate the source of problems. Demonstrates confidentiality regarding information pertaining to all students, faculty and staff. Maintains proper appearance and personal conduct for the employee’s particular job. Uses effective communication skills taking into consideration body language, filters, listening, paraphrasing, and questions with all customers. Demonstrates ability to work in a team environment. Ability to interpret and follow written schematics and blueprints. Good communication and customer service skills and the ability to communicate with a diverse campus population. Able to complete a University Drivers Safety Course as well as other OSHA required training programs. This role requires a strong commitment to workplace safety and the adherence to all established safety protocols. This includes, but is not limited to, proper use of personal protective equipment, reporting unsafe conditions, participating in safety training and actively promoting a culture of safety within the team. Failing to adhere to safety regulations can have serious consequences, including disciplinary action. Comfortable working at heights of up to 50 ft. using ladders scaffolds and high lifts. Able to work in confined spaces. Must be able to lift 40 lbs. on a regular basis. Ability to stoop, bend, crouch frequently for prolonged periods. WORKING CONDITIONS Exposure to varied indoor and outdoor working and weather conditions on a regular basis.  May be required to work weekends or overtime when needed. PHYSICAL ACTIVITIES _x_Climbing  _x_Balancing  _x_Stooping  _x_Kneeling  _x_Crouching  _x_Crawling  _x_Reaching  _x_Standing _x_Walking  _x_Pushing  _x_Pulling  _x_Lifting  _x_Grasping  _x_Feeling  _x_Talking  _x_Hearing _X_Repetitive motion PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS __Sedentary work  __Light work  __Medium work  _x_Heavy work  __Very Heavy work   __Visual acuity APPLICATION PROCESS To apply, please upload with your paycom application your resume, cover letter, 3 references and a copy of your license (Oregon Building Codes Division issued LME or LEB Electrical and Universal CFC Refrigeration .) along with your Paycom application.  Persons who do not follow and complete the application process are not applicants and will not be considered for employment. Only qualified applicants will be contacted for an interview. During the selection process, we will strive to provide timely notifications. The selection process may vary from recruitment to recruitment but typically includes multiple interviews and may take several weeks depending on the position. All qualified applicants will be notified once the selection process has closed. Offers of employment at Pacific University are contingent upon proof of eligibility to work in the United States. At Pacific University, we are dedicated to offering experiences that are authentic, holistic, equity-minded, and responsive. Our communal success rests on the recognition that complex problems and effective solutions are best approached by teams with a variety of diverse perspectives. and life experiences. As we continue to develop our equity practices, we actively promote access to opportunities and equitable pay for all employees. We, who make up Pacific University, aspire to become a community of purpose where everyone is enabled to be wholly and comfortably who they are; accountable for inclusive behaviors and practices; built on trust, civility, care, openness, and honest conversations often around critical subjects. We know that these values are critical to prepare for a global world with complex problems, through an asset-based mindset so that every one is afforded an opportunity to succeed. We believe in fostering a workplace where every employee is respected, their contributions are valued, and they are provided opportunities to succeed. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS We offer a comprehensive benefits package for qualifying employees. Current benefits include: Generous paid time off (for vacation, holidays—including winter break—and sick leave) Medical coverage with alternative care options (with in-network services covered at 100% after payroll deduction) Comprehensive dental and vision plans Generous retirement contribution after one year of service with no match required Free mental health appointments Tuition remission for employees and their dependent child(ren) who meet eligibility requirements On-campus benefits, including free access to our sports facility and library Discounts on campus food, bookstore purchases, clinic services, and outdoor program gear rentals (including kayaks, snowshoes, and bikes) EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYMENT Pacific University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to complying with all applicable laws, including those concerning employment and workplace policies. We are committed to fostering a non-discriminatory and inclusive work environment. We are proud to encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds, including those from historically underrepresented groups. NOTICE OF NONDISCRIMINATION POLICY Pacific University makes all employment decisions without regard to race, color, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, age, religion or religious creed, disability, sex, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other characteristics protected by applicable law. Applicable laws include, but are not limited to, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination Act, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990. Questions or complaints may be directed to the Vice President for Academic Affairs at 2043 College Way, Forest Grove, OR 97116 or v ia email at provost@pacificu.edu . Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/ABFDAFED645B6920CFDB8559C078F8A5/jobs/348823": {
      "title": "Athletics Annual Giving Coordinator",
      "description": "Athletics Annual Giving Coordinator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Athletics Annual Giving Coordinator Forest Grove Campus - Forest Grove, OR 97116; Hillsboro Professional Campus - Hillsboro, OR 97123-4218 Apply Overview Salary Range $45,000.00 - $50,000.00 Position Type Non-Exempt Category Faculty and Staff Apply Description Pacific University achieves excellence and distinction by investing in exceptional people to think, care, create, and pursue justice in our world. We embrace discovery in a close and nurturing environment that leads to genuine transformation. Our community is diverse, sustainable, and dedicated to discovery and excellence in teaching, scholarship, and practice. At Pacific University, we thrive in an extraordinary environment, surrounded by the beauty of the great Pacific Northwest, with campus locations in Forest Grove and Hillsboro. We humbly acknowledge and thank the original caretakers of the lands on which we live, work, teach, and acquire and share knowledge. GENERAL DESCRIPTION OF POSITION: Pacific University seeks a motivated and detail-oriented Athletics Annual Giving Coordinator to support the planning and execution of annual fundraising efforts benefiting Pacific Athletics. This entry-level role provides hands-on experience in donor engagement, digital fundraising, stewardship, and data-informed outreach strategies. The coordinator supports annual giving campaigns, giving days, donor call programs, and athletics-specific appeals and fundraising events, while also assisting with emerging technologies and AI-enabled tools designed to enhance donor engagement and participation. Working collaboratively with University Advancement and Athletics leadership, this role helps strengthen Boxer spirit and build a sustainable pipeline of athletics supporters. This is an excellent opportunity for an early-career professional seeking experience in higher education philanthropy, digital engagement strategy, and athletics fundraising. Salary Range: $45,000 - $50,000 Reports to: Director of Annual Giving ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS/MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES: Donor Retention & Growth Support implementation of strategies designed to increase athletics annual fund participation and improve donor retention year over year. Execute targeted renewal outreach to athletics donors, including segmented email, calls, fundraising events, and digital engagement efforts. Assist in identifying and engaging new athletics donors to expand the annual giving base. Giving Day & Campaign Performance Coordinate athletics participation in university-wide giving days and annual campaigns, with a focus on increasing donor count and sport-specific engagement. Support execution of sport-specific appeals aligned with institutional fundraising goals. Track participation metrics and assist in reporting on campaign performance. Engagement & Stewardship Collaborate with Athletics and Advancement to integrate donor cultivation and stewardship opportunities into athletic events. Support timely acknowledgment and recognition efforts to strengthen donor experience and retention. Compliance & Collaboration Operate within NCAA guidelines and institutional compliance standards. Partner with Annual Giving, Alumni Engagement, and Athletics leadership to align outreach strategies and engagement efforts. Annual Giving Support: Digital & Direct Outreach Support execution of digital fundraising campaigns, including segmented email, social media, and AI-assisted outreach. Participate in call-down and texting initiatives to secure annual gifts and increase alumni and parent participation. Contribute to strategies that increase overall annual giving participation rates. Data & Performance Tracking Maintain accurate donor records and contact reports in the CRM. Assist in tracking key performance indicators, including donor count, retention rate, participation rate, and campaign progress. Provide regular updates on outreach metrics and engagement results. Stewardship & Communications Draft and coordinate donor acknowledgments and annual giving communications. Support impact reporting and recognition efforts for athletics donors. SECONDARY FUNCTIONS: Support the planning and execution of broader University Advancement fundraising campaigns and engagement initiatives as assigned. Assist in tracking campaign progress and compiling data to measure participation, retention, and overall effectiveness. Prepare summary reports and dashboards to support performance analysis and strategic decision-making. Provide responsive donor relations support by managing phone and email inquiries in a timely and professional manner. Assist with event logistics and donor engagement activities that support cultivation and stewardship goals. JOB SCOPE: This position operates with a moderate degree of independence within established University Advancement strategies and institutional policies. The coordinator executes assigned initiatives, manages defined outreach efforts, and exercises sound judgment in day-to-day decision-making. Complex or high-level strategic decisions are escalated to the supervisor as appropriate. SUPERVISOR RESPONSIBILITY: This position does not have formal supervisory responsibilities but may assist in coordinating student workers or volunteers during campaign or event activities. Qualifications REQUIRED EDUCATION AND/OR EXPERIENCE: Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. Prior experience in athletics, fundraising, marketing, or customer engagement is preferred but not required. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Demonstrated interest in philanthropy, higher education advancement, or athletics fundraising. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Excellent organizational skills with attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and familiarity with social media platforms. Comfort with technology and digital engagement tools; ability and willingness to learn fundraising CRM systems and AI-enabled outreach platforms. Ability to work effectively and professionally with students, faculty, staff, alumni, and external constituents. Ability to analyze basic data and track participation metrics to support fundraising performance goals. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Experience participating in or working with intercollegiate athletics programs. Prior experience in fundraising, sales, alumni relations, or customer engagement. Familiarity with NCAA rules and compliance considerations. Experience with CRM or donor management systems (e.g., Blackbaud, Salesforce, Almabase). Demonstrated interest in collegiate athletics culture and student-athlete success. WORKING CONDITIONS: This position is primarily based on Pacific University’s Forest Grove campus and may require occasional travel to the Hillsboro campus or other locations as needed. The role operates in a professional office environment but requires regular attendance at athletic events, competitions, donor gatherings, fundraising events, and stewardship activities. Evening and weekend work is required, particularly during athletic seasons, giving days, and peak campaign periods. WORK ENVIRONMENT: This position operates within a collaborative, fast-paced University Advancement environment that emphasizes performance, accountability, and donor-centered engagement. The Athletics Annual Giving Coordinator is expected to demonstrate professionalism, responsiveness, and sound judgment in all interactions with donors, alumni, student-athletes, coaches, and campus partners. The role requires flexibility, initiative, and the ability to adapt to changing priorities, particularly during athletic seasons and campaign cycles. A high level of integrity, discretion, and commitment to NCAA compliance and institutional policies is expected. Success in this position requires a team-oriented mindset, comfort engaging with diverse stakeholders, and enthusiasm for supporting Pacific University’s mission and the success of its student-athletes. HYBRID/REMOTE WORK ELIGIBILITY: ▪ Hybrid Schedule Expectations: Regular evening and/or weekend responsibilities Travel Requirements: Some travel required PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Primarily sedentary work, involving extended periods of sitting and computer use. Occasional medium work, including lifting or moving objects up to 50 pounds (e.g., event materials, signage, or equipment). Ability to walk, stand, climb stairs, and move between campus facilities and athletic venues. Visual acuity sufficient to review written materials, electronic data, and digital communications. APPLICATION PROCESS To apply, please upload your resume and cover letter along with your Paycom application.  Persons who do not follow and complete the application process are not applicants and will not be considered for employment. Only qualified applicants will be contacted for an interview. During the selection process, we will strive to provide timely notifications. The selection process may vary from recruitment to recruitment but typically includes multiple interviews and may take several weeks depending on the position. All qualified applicants will be notified once the selection process has closed. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and continue to work without employer visa sponsorship, now or in the future. At Pacific University, we are dedicated to offering experiences that are authentic, holistic, equity-minded, and responsive. Our communal success rests on the recognition that complex problems and effective solutions are best approached by teams with a variety of diverse perspectives. and life experiences. As we continue to develop our equity practices, we actively promote access to opportunities and equitable pay for all employees. Studies have shown that women and people of color are less likely to apply for jobs where they are unsure if they can perform every function in the job description. We are most interested in finding the best candidate for the job and that candidate may come from a variety of backgrounds and lived experiences. If you are interested in applying , we encourage you to think broadly about how your background and skill set may qualify you for the role. We, who make up Pacific University, aspire to become a community of purpose where everyone is enabled to be wholly and comfortably who they are; accountable for inclusive behaviors and practices; built on trust, civility, care, openness, and honest conversations often around critical subjects. We know that these values are critical to prepare for a global world with complex problems, through an asset-based mindset so that everyone is afforded an opportunity to succeed. We believe in fostering a workplace where every employee is respected, their contributions are valued, and they are provided opportunities to succeed. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS We offer a comprehensive benefits package for qualifying employees. Current benefits include: Generous paid time off (for vacation, holidays—including winter break—and sick leave) Medical coverage with alternative care options (with in-network services covered at 100% after payroll deduction) Comprehensive dental and vision plans Generous retirement contribution after one year of service with no match required Free mental health appointments Tuition remission for employees and their dependent child(ren) who meet eligibility requirements On-campus benefits, including free access to our sports facility and library Discounts on campus food, bookstore purchases, clinic services, and outdoor program gear rentals (including kayaks, snowshoes, and bikes) EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYMENT Pacific University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to complying with all applicable laws, including those concerning employment and workplace policies. We are committed to fostering a non-discriminatory and inclusive work environment. We are proud to encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds, including those from historically underrepresented groups. NOTICE OF NONDISCRIMINATION POLICY Pacific University makes all employment decisions without regard to race, color, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, age, religion or religious creed, disability, sex, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other characteristics protected by applicable law. Applicable laws include, but are not limited to, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination Act, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990. Questions or complaints may be directed to the Vice President for Academic Affairs at 2043 College Way, Forest Grove, OR 97116 or via email at provost@pacificu.edu . Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/ABFDAFED645B6920CFDB8559C078F8A5/jobs/348756": {
      "title": "Coordinator for Experiential Education & Student Services",
      "description": "Coordinator for Experiential Education & Student Services - Pharmacy You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Coordinator for Experiential Education & Student Services - Pharmacy Forest Grove Campus - Forest Grove, OR 97116 Apply Overview Salary Range $45,000.00 - $52,666.00 Position Type Non-Exempt Category Faculty and Staff Apply Description Pacific University achieves excellence and distinction by investing in exceptional people to think, care, create, and pursue justice in our world. We embrace discovery in a close and nurturing environment that leads to genuine transformation. Our community is diverse, sustainable, and dedicated to discovery and excellence in teaching, scholarship, and practice. At Pacific University, we thrive in an extraordinary environment, surrounded by the beauty of the great Pacific Northwest, with campus locations in Forest Grove and Hillsboro. We humbly acknowledge and thank the original caretakers of the lands on which we live, work, teach, and acquire and share knowledge. POSITION DESCRIPTION This position shares duties and responsibilities between the Office of Experiential Education (OEE) and the Office of Student Affairs (OSA) It is a shared position supervised by the Assistant Dean for Experiential Education (ADEE). The allocation of effort between the two areas is 60% OEE) / 40% OSA. The annual evaluation will be conducted by the primary supervisor, the Assistant Dean for Experiential Education (ADEE), in collaboration with the Assistant Dean for Student Affairs (ADSA). DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES (A) Office of Student Affairs Duties (40%): Assist the Assistant Dean for Student Affairs (ADSA) and faculty mentors in supporting student leadership development initiatives through coordination of pharmacy student organizations. Assist in the development, implementation, and administration of policies related to student leadership programs and student organization activities: Coordinate and provide administrative support for faculty and peer mentorship programs in collaboration with the ADSA. Assist in development, maintenance, and communication of University and School resources available to students Support planning and implementation of Office of Student Affairs events and community outreach, including but not limited to Student Admission Days, White Coat Ceremony, Graduate Awards & Hooding Ceremony, Orientation Week, P3 Return to Campus Week, Annual Career and Experiential Fair, Annual Research Showcase, and other events supporting PharmD and MSPS students in the School of Pharmacy. Coordinate the School’s participation in the annual First Destination Survey in collaboration with the Office of Institutional Research. Track student response rates for job placement and post- graduation outcome data collection and prepare reports for the Dean. Collaborate with the ADSA, ADAA, and the Assessment and Quality Improvement Committee (AQUIC) in analyzing student outcomes data and supporting program improvement initiatives. Coordinate opportunities for on-campus speakers from community partners, professional organizations, and potential employers including maintenance of the School of Pharmacy Job Board. (B) Office of Experiential Education Duties (55%): Manage student records for both matriculation and experiential education requirements. Verify submission and completion of required documentation from students and preceptors (e.g., vaccination records, evaluation forms, pre-rotation paperwork, and other materials). Serve as the primary point of contact for students, preceptors, and site coordinators regarding platforms used for student tracking Provide secondary administrative support to the Director of Experiential Education (DEE) for clinical onboarding documentation processes. Coordinate annual and as-needed recertification requirements for P1–P3 students, including intern licenses, HIPAA training, bloodborne pathogen (BBP) training, BLS certification, TB testing, immunizations, drug screening, and background checks. Facilitate the execution, renewal, and revision of affiliation agreements with experiential sites. Provide administrative coordination for the Global Experience Exchange Program. Manage dissemination of certificates for Oregon Board of Pharmacy–approved continuing education (CE) programs offered by the School of Pharmacy. Assist the Office of Experiential Education (OEE) with annual updates to the Preceptor Manual and the Experiential Education section of the Student Handbook. Support the development, management, and maintenance of experiential education databases, including site and preceptor contact information and onboarding requirements. Collaborate with the ADEE, ADSA, and Senior Administrative Assistant (SAA) in planning and implementing the annual Career and Experiential Fair (C) Other Duties (5%) Perform other duties as assigned by the Dean, ADSA, and ADEE, including service to the School, College, and University. Qualifications POSITION QUALIFICATIONS Associate’s degree required; a Bachelor’s degree preferred. Relevant professional experience in related fields may be considered in lieu of a degree. At least one year of experience in project management is desirable Ability to manage responsibilities independently and perform tasks with minimal supervision. Demonstrated experience in customer service or student-facing support roles. Experience in the pharmacy field, healthcare, or higher education environment is preferred. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications (Word, Excel) is required Experience working with databases is desirable Demonstrated ability to learn and effectively use new technology platforms and software applications. Ability to work effectively with individuals from culturally diverse backgrounds, including students of color, international students, non-traditional students, and returning learners, and to foster cultural awareness and inclusive practices within a university community. Strong interpersonal and teamwork skills with the ability to communicate effectively and collaborate with administrators, faculty, students, and external partners. Highly organized with strong attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously. Demonstrated professionalism in interactions with both internal and external stakeholders. Ability to maintain strict confidentiality regarding sensitive information related to students, faculty, and staff in compliance with applicable regulations (e.g., FERPA, HIPAA). Demonstrated initiative in evaluating processes, identifying opportunities for improvement, and proposing solutions to enhance efficiency and operational integrity within the School of Pharmacy. APPLICATION PROCESS To apply, please upload your resume, cover letter and three professional references along with your Paycom application. Persons who do not follow and complete the application process are not applicants and will not be considered for employment. Only qualified applicants will be contacted for an interview. During the selection process, we will strive to provide timely notifications. The selection process may vary from recruitment to recruitment but typically includes multiple interviews and may take several weeks depending on the position. All qualified applicants will be notified once the selection process has closed. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and continue to work without employer visa sponsorship, now or in the future. At Pacific University, we are dedicated to offering experiences that are authentic, holistic, equity-minded, and responsive. Our communal success rests on the recognition that complex problems and effective solutions are best approached by teams with a variety of diverse perspectives. and life experiences. As we continue to develop our equity practices, we actively promote access to opportunities and equitable pay for all employees. Studies have shown that women and people of color are less likely to apply for jobs where they are unsure if they can perform every function in the job description. We are most interested in finding the best candidate for the job and that candidate may come from a variety of backgrounds and lived experiences. If you are interested in applying, we encourage you to think broadly about how your background and skill set may qualify you for the role. We, who make up Pacific University, aspire to become a community of purpose where everyone is enabled to be wholly and comfortably who they are; accountable for inclusive behaviors and practices; built on trust, civility, care, openness, and honest conversations often around critical subjects. We know that these values are critical to prepare for a global world with complex problems, through an asset-based mindset so that everyone is afforded an opportunity to succeed. We believe in fostering a workplace where every employee is respected, their contributions are valued, and they are provided opportunities to succeed. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS We offer a comprehensive benefits package for qualifying employees. Current benefits include: Generous paid time off (for vacation, holidays—including winter break—and sick leave) Medical coverage with alternative care options (with in-network services covered at 100% after payroll deduction) Comprehensive dental and vision plans Generous retirement contribution after one year of service with no match required Free mental health appointments Tuition remission for employees and their dependent child(ren) who meet eligibility requirements On-campus benefits, including free access to our sports facility and library Discounts on campus food, bookstore purchases, clinic services. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYMENT Pacific University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to complying with all applicable laws, including those concerning employment and workplace policies. We are committed to fostering a non-discriminatory and inclusive work environment. We are proud to encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds, including those from historically underrepresented groups. NOTICE OF NONDISCRIMINATION POLICY Pacific University makes all employment decisions without regard to race, color, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, age, religion or religious creed, disability, sex, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other characteristics protected by applicable law. Applicable laws include, but are not limited to, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination Act, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990. Questions or complaints may be directed to the Vice President for Academic Affairs at 2043 College Way, Forest Grove, OR 97116 or via email at provost@pacificu.edu . Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
